    "media:imagetext": "THESATURDAY EVENING POSTI\nFebruary 1s a\nERNEST HEMINGWAY says:\n\"Each generation of Americans\n...Why? Because you'll see your own\nSigned at the Finca Vigia, Cuba. Dec. 1st, 1955\nneeds to re discover Europe\ncountry's destiny more clearly if you spend your next vacation abroad\"\n\"Pau AmErican and I are old friends\"\n\"We started flying commercially about the same\ntime. They did the flying and I was the passenger.\nIt turned out to be a good partnership.\n\"After the old Key West-Miami-Havana-Bahamas\nearly days, there was the Pacific when you took a\nday to Midway-another to Wake-one more to\nGuam-one to Manila-then Hongkong.\n\"Flying in China you had to sweat out many\nthings. But you never worried about equipment,\nmaintenance nor any Pan American pilot. I feel as\nsafe with Pan American as I do any morning I wake\nup to a good working day.\"\nOnly Pan American offers overnight service from\nNew York, Boston, Philadelphia, Detroit, and Chicago\nto 25 European cities... Fly Now-Pay Later!\nFLY NOW-PAY LATER\nPan American originated \"Pay Later\" and\nnow-thru March 3-has a new money.\nsaving Family Fare plan. Ask for details.\nTourist\n20 monthly\ndown payment\nShannon.\nLondon..\n44\n49\nParis..\nFrankfort.\nRome...\nNice.\nIstanbul..\n79\n'Round the World... 135\nThe Romans tried, but couldn't bridge the mighty\nfloods of the Rhône River at Avignon. Here in the\nSouth of France in the vear 1177. Saint Benezeg\nbuilt the famous stone bridge which lasted until\nPAN AMERICAN\nWORLD'S MOST EXPERIENCED AIRLINE\n1680. Today, in a morning's drive from the Pan\nAmerican airport at Nice, you can be dancing be-\nfore lunch on the bridge where seven generations of\nAmericans have sung. \"On v danse tout en ronde.\"",
